WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.310
Hi. I'm Gus Halwani.

2
00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:05.630
I've followed one thread
for most of my life.

3
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.370
It started with sound.

4
00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.330
I trained as a sound engineer.

5
00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.980
Then I got curious about what
the brain does with sound,

6
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.370
so I went to MIT and did my
doctorate in neuroscience.

7
00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:21.350
I used brain imaging —
MRI, DTI and fMRI —

8
00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.950
to study how musicians' brains
differ from non-musicians',

9
00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:28.010
and what that could mean
for recovery after a stroke.

10
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:32.310
After that, I went into learning,
and into building things.

11
00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:36.010
I was Chief Innovation Officer
at The Possible Zone, in Boston.

12
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.470
I built sensors for race car drivers.

13
00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.340
I co-founded a startup
that makes visual stories

14
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.810
for neurodivergent kids
and their families.

15
00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:46.890
So what do I do now? Two things.

16
00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.950
One: creative work.

17
00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:54.310
I develop ideas, and I make images,
film, sound, and interactive work.

18
00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:57.150
Two: technology, and change.

19
00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:01.730
I help organizations choose new
technology and actually use it.

20
00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.870
Sometimes that's designing a product.

21
00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:05.810
Sometimes it's leading the build.

22
00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:09.170
Sometimes it's helping a
team change how it works.

23
00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:13.890
I take on select speaking engagements,
workshops, and project work.

24
00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.650
If that sounds like you,
reach out through the site.

25
00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:18.610
I'd like to hear what
you're working on.
